    "lastText": "The spreadsheet engine is built and the goal's audit returned VERDICT: PASS. All 42 acceptance criteria pass, and `npm test` runs 99 tests with 0 failures.\n\n**What's in the project**\n- `src/sheet.js` — the `Sheet` class, with a tokenizer, a precedence-climbing parser, a lazy evaluator, static cycle analysis for `#CIRC!`, and the full function table (52 functions).\n- `test/*.test.js` — 20 test files, one per group of criteria, each written from the TASK.md rules.\n- `README.md` — API, operators, error rules, and every function.\n- `package.json` — `npm test` runs `node --test`; no dependencies.\n- `.goal/SPEC.md` — 42 criteria, each with a verify command.\n\n**Decisions I made where TASK.md was open**\n- Cycle detection uses static references: a cell is `#CIRC!` if it sits on a cycle or reads one, even when `IF` would skip the loop.\n- Booleans in literals must match exactly (`TRUE`/`FALSE` in any case, no surrounding spaces); numeric literals may have surrounding spaces.\n- `AND`/`OR`/`XOR` with no logical values give `#VALUE!`; `PRODUCT` of nothing gives 0.\n- Errors in ranges propagate, including through `COUNTA` and `ISBLANK`, following the spec's \"any function that receives an error argument\" rule.\n- `ISNUMBER`, `ISTEXT`, `ISBLANK` and `ISLOGICAL` propagate errors. Only `ISERROR`, `ISNA`, `IFERROR` and `IFNA` take errors as input.\n\n**Spec additions after the freeze**\nThe first audit failed on coverage: reversed ranges (`SUM(A3:A1)`) and `$` markers inside formulas had no criterion or test. I added AC-41 and AC-42 with a new test file, and recorded the addition in SPEC.md. Nothing was removed or reworded.\n\n**Audit history**\nThe first audit returned FAIL on those coverage gaps. The re-audit after the additions returned PASS. An earlier auditor agent may still send a late notification; its result is superseded by the PASS above.",
